// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
//
// The ignore list the publishing host's sync folder carries.
//
// 🚨 **This is the sync-layer half of the publish boundary, and it is belt to the server's
// suspenders — both wear it.** The server refuses to serve anything outside its publish
// boundary even if this file were empty; this file is what keeps the internal material
// from ever *arriving* on a machine whose only job is to be public. Two independent
// enforcement points, because the consequences are asymmetric: the boundary refusing at
// serve time is one bug away from a leak; the bytes never landing is not a bug away from
// anything.
//
// ⚠️ **Keep this file and the boundary's defaults in step.** The boundary decides what the
// *server* will serve; this decides what the *folder* will hold. If you widen one and not
// the other, the wider one is your true boundary — write that down rather than discovering
// it in a log.
//
// Syntax: Syncthing's ignore patterns (https://docs.syncthing.net/users/ignoring), one
// per line, and **the FIRST pattern that matches decides a file's fate** — so every
// negation stands ABOVE the general exclude that would otherwise match its subject, and
// directories re-included against a starred exclude need their contents negated too,
// because the star's expanded form matches everything under its children. `(?d)` marks a
// pattern safe to delete files over — everything here is, because nothing on this machine
// is authoritative.

// The re-inclusions first: the public task root (the board is published copy) and the
// board base (the only .base file the server allowlists).
!/00-09 Metafiles/01 Tasks
!/00-09 Metafiles/01 Tasks/**
!/Anthers Tasks.base

(?d)/Internal Wiki
(?d)/90-99 Agents

// 00-09 Metafiles: vault machinery — attachments, templates, the task-tooling files.
// The star covers the folder's direct children and (expanded) everything under them,
// except what the negations above re-include.
(?d)/00-09 Metafiles/*

// Obsidian, sync and agent machinery.
(?d)/.obsidian
(?d)/.agents
(?d)/.trash
(?d)/.stfolder
(?d)/.stversions

// Root-level base files other than the board (the server also refuses them).
// (// comments, never # — a bare # line is a pattern to Syncthing, not a comment.)
(?d)/*.base